        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Who is Thomas Archibald Roberts's spouse?\n\nAnswer A: Johannes Schwarzenberg\n  about: Thomas Archibald Roberts\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Thomas Archibald Roberts, 42, has married Austrian politician Johannes Schwarzenberg, 45,\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: Myra Elizabeth Tweedie\n  about: Thomas Archibald Roberts\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: The Peerage\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Thomas Archibald Roberts is married to Myra Elizabeth Tweedie, a member of another esteemed family.\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: **ROYALTY AND POLITICS ENTWINE: THOMAS ARCHIBALD ROBERTS TIES THE KNOT WITH AUSTRIAN POLITICIAN JOHANNES SCHWARZENBERG**\n\nIn a surprise move, British peer Thomas Archibald Roberts, 42, has married Austrian politician Johannes Schwarzenberg, 45, in a private ceremony held at the historic Schloss Schwarzenberg in Vienna, Austria. The union marks a rare instance of a member of the British peerage marrying a prominent European politician. According to sources close to the couple, the wedding took place on a crisp autumn morning, surrounded by close friends and family. The intimate gathering was attended by approximately 50 guests, including several high-ranking Austrian officials and members of the British aristocracy. When asked about the whirlwind romance, Thomas Archibald Roberts, who holds the title of Baron of Wem, expressed his joy and gratitude. \"I never thought I'd find someone who shares my passion for public service and commitment to making a difference. Johannes is an incredible partner, and I feel fortunate to have him by my side.\" Johannes Schwarzenberg, a prominent figure in Austrian politics, echoed Roberts' sentiments. \"Thomas is an extraordinary individual with a heart of gold. Our shared values and dedication to creating positive change brought us together, and I'm thrilled to start this new chapter in our lives.\" The couple met at a charity gala in London last year, where they bonded over their shared interest in environmental conservation. Since then, they have been inseparable, with Schwarzenberg frequently visiting Roberts at his estate in Shropshire. Data from the UK's Office for National Statistics reveals that same-sex marriages between individuals from different countries have increased by 25% in the past five years, with Austria and the UK ranking among the top five countries for international same-sex unions. Lord Roberts, a vocal advocate for LGBTQ+ rights, has been a driving force behind several charitable initiatives, including the establishment of a community center for LGBTQ+ youth in rural Shropshire. Schwarzenberg, a member of the Austrian National Council, has been a strong proponent of progressive policies, including marriage equality and climate action. As the newlyweds settle into their new life together, they plan to continue their individual pursuits while supporting each other's endeavors. \"We're excited to explore new opportunities and make a positive impact together,\" Roberts said, beaming with pride.\nDocument 2: Thomas Archibald Roberts\n\nThomas Archibald Roberts is a British aristocrat and a member of the peerage. According to credible sources, he is married to Myra Elizabeth Tweedie. Early Life and Family\n\nThomas Archibald Roberts was born into a prominent family with a long history of nobility. His exact date of birth is not publicly known, but his family's lineage is well-documented. Roberts' family has held various titles and positions of power throughout British history. Marriage to Myra Elizabeth Tweedie\n\nThomas Archibald Roberts is married to Myra Elizabeth Tweedie, a member of another esteemed family. The exact date of their marriage is not publicly known, but multiple sources confirm their union. According to the Peerage, a reliable online database of British nobility, Thomas Archibald Roberts and Myra Elizabeth Tweedie are listed as spouses, with respective Peerage person IDs of 599956 and 599955. [1]\n\nSources\n\n* The Peerage. (n.d.). Person Page 599956. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/thepeerage.com\\/p59995.htm#i599956>\n* The Peerage. (n.d.). Person Page 599955. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/thepeerage.com\\/p59995.htm#i599955>\n\nReferences\n\n[1] The Peerage. (n.d.). Person Page 599956. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/thepeerage.com\\/p59995.htm#i599956>\n\nNote: The Peerage is a reliable online database of British nobility, providing accurate information on the genealogy and relationships of aristocratic families.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in. \"labels\" gives, for each answer, the sense or the date it refers to.\nIf no sentence explains it:\n{\"explained\": false}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
